Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.20,0:00:18.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.80,0:00:26.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Mila?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.93,0:00:32.47,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,My words hold no magic...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.47,0:00:34.88,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It's been a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.88,0:00:37.00,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I see you took the throne with no issues.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.51,0:00:38.54,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Valt?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.74,0:00:42.54,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Who in the world {\i1}are{\i0} you?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.16,0:02:18.99,Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Joyful Sorrow ~
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.10,0:02:24.04,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I didn't expect you to absorb \NSimila's physical components.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.53,0:02:27.16,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You're the one who manifested Simila?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.46,0:02:28.68,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.68,0:02:34.42,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,But it was Cezar who decided \Nto sacrifice their own men.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.09,0:02:36.52,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,You should sit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.52,0:02:37.67,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'm sure you're tired.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.16,0:02:40.87,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Oh, would you like a change of clothes?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.30,0:02:43.71,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I can't get changed like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.71,0:02:44.64,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.64,0:02:48.10,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Only the Farsas royal family can undo that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.45,0:02:53.03,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,My grandfather borrowed it \Nfrom the Farsas treasury...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.50,0:02:56.83,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,to use on you, once you came to this era.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.57,0:02:58.32,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.74,0:03:01.87,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,You seem alert now, so let me get to the point.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.68,0:03:03.69,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,You see, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.69,0:03:06.96,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,No, {\i1}we{\i0} are after Eleterria.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.36,0:03:09.26,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,The red and blue magic spheres.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.26,0:03:11.75,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,We want you to bring both of them to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.43,0:03:13.90,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,How do you...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.90,0:03:15.50,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Know about them?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.50,0:03:18.36,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Or how do we plan to use them?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.17,0:03:22.10,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'm plenty knowledgeable in these matters.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.10,0:03:23.68,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,More than you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.85,0:03:28.36,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What do you plan to change \Nonce you've obtained them?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.36,0:03:29.89,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I can't tell you yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.35,0:03:32.63,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,If you choose to cooperate...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.22,0:03:38.12,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.51,0:03:40.53,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.90,0:03:42.21,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Search the premises!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.21,0:03:42.92,Default,Group,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.58,0:03:48.08,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I really can't let my eyes off you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.54,0:03:49.95,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.40,0:03:51.81,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.81,0:03:54.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's a sealing ornament from your country.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.26,0:03:56.67,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I believe it works the same way as Akashia.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.93,0:04:00.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Is this the artifact stolen from \Nour treasury forty years ago?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.41,0:04:03.64,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,How did you find me here?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.64,0:04:07.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I scoured all of Cezar with the barrier \Nyou placed on me as a guide.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.87,0:04:09.14,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}You{\i0} did?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.14,0:04:10.79,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Even though the war just ended?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.21,0:04:13.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Well, my body was the key to detecting you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.21,0:04:15.93,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.09,0:04:19.01,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Um, how's Sylvia doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.01,0:04:20.08,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Nothing severe.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.08,0:04:23.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She should be back on her feet \Nin a couple days or so.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.04,0:04:25.48,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Let us return.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.03,0:04:27.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't want to worry those waiting for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.32,0:04:35.58,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So they really are after the orbs...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.58,0:04:38.56,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But why would they need both of them?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.56,0:04:39.92,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Beats me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.92,0:04:42.42,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Maybe there's a different way they can be used.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.11,0:04:47.76,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We'll look into it on our end, but you \Nshould stay on guard for the time being.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.76,0:04:49.20,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,They're targeting you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.62,0:04:50.68,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.24,0:04:58.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Also, you saved us from that evil god.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.10,0:04:59.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.26,0:05:09.03,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Your Majesty! Is now a good time?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.79,0:05:11.21,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Obviously not.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.25,0:05:15.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So? What do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.85,0:05:19.12,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,We received a visit from a woman \Nasking to meet Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.12,0:05:20.38,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Who?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.38,0:05:21.59,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.44,0:05:23.79,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,I'm not sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.72,0:05:42.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Where are my guards?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.69,0:05:48.66,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)\pos(427,290)}Lavinia    {\fs14}Witch of Silence
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.58,0:05:49.46,Default-Top,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I see my curse has been expertly broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.30,0:05:52.83,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Is the Witch Killer Queen responsible?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.72,0:05:54.79,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Your voice...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.99,0:05:59.85,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You're the Witch of Silence!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.85,0:06:01.40,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Long time no see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.40,0:06:02.63,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,You've grown.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.98,0:06:04.63,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Enough of your prattle.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.63,0:06:05.84,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Why are you here?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.84,0:06:08.30,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I was going to let you off with just the curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.30,0:06:10.43,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,How incorrigible.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.43,0:06:12.56,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I'm left with no choice \Nnow that it's been broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.73,0:06:14.89,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Lazar! Run for it!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.57,0:06:21.77,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Mila! Karr!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.77,0:06:24.09,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,An interesting means of \Nprotection you have there.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.09,0:06:26.07,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,The work of your lovely bride?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.69,0:06:27.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It ends here!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.74,0:06:29.21,Default,Kevin,0,0,0,,Don't kill her, Oscar!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.27,0:06:34.31,Default,Kevin,0,0,0,,That's...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.21,0:06:36.58,Default,Kevin,0,0,0,,your grandmother.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.90,0:06:39.92,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Succumb to dreams from childhood.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.06,0:07:10.53,Flashback,Lazar,0,0,0,,What are you doing out here, Your Highness?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.05,0:07:13.24,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,I just stepped out for a moment, Lazar.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.79,0:07:15.79,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,And stop calling me Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.79,0:07:17.45,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,It feels weird.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.79,0:07:20.91,Flashback,Lazar,0,0,0,,Your Highness is Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.94,0:07:41.35,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,Ettard, it's time for today's training.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.35,0:07:45.71,Flashback,Ettard,0,0,0,,There's not much more I can teach you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.71,0:07:47.07,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,No need to be humble.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.07,0:07:48.51,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,Please be my sparring partner.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.51,0:07:50.07,Flashback,Ettard,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.11,0:07:55.53,Flashback,Ettard,0,0,0,,Sometime next year, an energetic pupil \Nof mine should arrive at the palace.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.53,0:07:59.25,Flashback,Ettard,0,0,0,,His name is Als, and he's four years \Nolder than Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.25,0:08:01.17,Flashback,Ettard,0,0,0,,He's quite the skilled fighter.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.17,0:08:03.00,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,Now that sounds exciting.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.26,0:08:52.09,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar, draw Akashia.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.65,0:08:55.47,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.30,0:09:00.09,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Draw Akashia from its scabbard, Oscar.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.10,0:09:02.04,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.51,0:09:06.98,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's okay. Have faith.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.83,0:09:19.16,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.30,0:09:21.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Have you come to?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.96,0:09:25.25,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,That can't be.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.94,0:09:28.72,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,No one should be able to overwrite my spell.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.72,0:09:32.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I can't overwrite it, but I can exploit it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.76,0:09:35.67,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I inserted my own dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.67,0:09:38.89,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,My spell should only show childhood dreams.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.89,0:09:41.22,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That happens to be a childhood dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.02,0:09:44.85,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Don't think too much about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.40,0:09:58.36,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,You would have been happier \Nif you'd stayed asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.94,0:10:01.45,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It's meaningless if I'm the only one happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.19,0:10:05.29,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,You are the child that must die...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.81,0:10:08.29,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,to bring balance to the fate that was altered.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.29,0:10:09.91,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,"The child that must die"?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.47,0:10:12.50,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Is that why you cast that curse on me?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.50,0:10:13.82,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.82,0:10:16.02,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,The one you should condemn is your mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.13,0:10:39.78,Flashback,Rosalia,0,0,0,,Oscar!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.79,0:11:01.42,Flashback,Rosalia,0,0,0,,Thank goodness...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.87,0:11:10.96,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.02,0:11:14.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I will not condemn my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.90,0:11:16.50,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She defended me with her life.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.90,0:11:18.48,Default,Kevin,0,0,0,,So you remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.13,0:11:21.32,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thanks to that dream earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.83,0:11:31.18,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,Mother...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.76,0:11:41.76,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)\pos(434,290)}Rosalia    {\fs14}Oscar's Mother
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.71,0:11:42.47,Flashback-Top,Rosalia,0,0,0,,What's the matter, Oscar?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.23,0:11:47.34,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.13,0:11:51.98,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Mother went to the past to save my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.92,0:11:55.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You're my grandmother?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.50,0:11:58.01,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I {\i1}do{\i0} see a resemblance.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.65,0:12:01.24,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You sealed away my memories, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.63,0:12:04.95,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,You were the one who should have died.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.04,0:12:10.71,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,The demonic spirit attacked you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.90,0:12:15.96,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,But Rosalia could not accept that reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.60,0:12:22.99,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,She committed the sin of using \Na magic sphere to distort the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.93,0:12:28.64,Default,Rosalia,0,0,0,,Oscar!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.57,0:12:35.56,Default,Kevin,0,0,0,,Rosalia returned to before you were \Nattacked and managed to save your life.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.62,0:12:37.48,Default,Kevin,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.50,0:12:43.39,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Rosalia ended up dying instead, \Nwhich complicated matters.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.95,0:12:48.41,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Even if the past is successfully altered, \Nit does not change the user's death.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.15,0:12:53.75,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Rosalia's lifespan was set the moment \Nshe traded blows with the spirit,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.75,0:12:55.64,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,and when that moment arrived...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.83,0:13:01.80,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,She died without any warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.81,0:13:08.55,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,As a result, Rosalia saved your life, \Nbut killed your psyche.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.27,0:13:14.27,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,You deserve neither blame nor hatred.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.56,0:13:18.23,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,That said, you are someone \Nwho should not be alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.10,0:13:23.69,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Which is why your blood \Nmust not be passed down.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.57,0:13:28.67,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If you seek retribution for my mother's \Ndeeds, I will readily take you on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.09,0:13:31.13,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,After all, I did the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.02,0:13:39.36,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,The Witch Killer...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.13,0:13:44.05,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Is the reason you entered \Nthe childhood dream...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.55,0:13:46.36,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I see now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.81,0:13:49.75,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,You fools!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.75,0:13:50.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.51,0:13:51.47,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.01,0:14:01.73,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Why do you add to your sins?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.73,0:14:02.69,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Relive them?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.99,0:14:06.69,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Your actions may have had dire consequences.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.69,0:14:09.41,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The current me can't answer those questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.41,0:14:14.51,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,But if she was suffering, \Nand I had the means...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.24,0:14:17.32,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I would save her no matter what.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.78,0:14:21.21,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Be it me who altered the past, \Nor some other force...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.09,0:14:24.31,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The present is what matters to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.67,0:14:27.88,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Even if it ends up warping this world?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.88,0:14:31.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Even so, I'll move forward from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.26,0:14:32.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Right now is all I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.58,0:14:39.39,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It may be absurd to say while pointing this \Nat you, but I don't want you to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.39,0:14:42.36,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I suppose it's asking for too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.36,0:14:44.79,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,It really is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.79,0:14:46.26,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Greed beyond selfishness.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.61,0:14:51.70,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,She lifted the curse for you, \Nand now you seek to take her as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.70,0:14:56.91,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If that curse is what drew her to me, \Nperhaps I should be thanking you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.76,0:15:01.39,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,That woman is practically a witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.39,0:15:05.73,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,If she bears your child, \Nthat child will be a witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.73,0:15:09.25,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Is she so precious that you would \Nmarry her with that knowledge?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.25,0:15:10.03,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She is.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.15,0:15:12.46,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Raising a witch as my child?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.99,0:15:14.64,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I do love a challenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.88,0:15:20.22,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,How in the world did you raise him?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.22,0:15:22.11,Default,Kevin,0,0,0,,He's always been like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.53,0:15:27.94,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,The day may come when you \Nwish you'd killed me here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.94,0:15:30.51,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If it does, I'll kill you then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.33,0:15:39.68,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Do as you like, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.69,0:15:43.94,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,But do take care not to \Ncommit any more follies,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.02,0:15:48.33,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,lest the time come when you \Nneed to balance everything out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.71,0:15:51.19,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll keep that in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.85,0:16:12.65,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,How unwary of you, \Nafter what happened yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.92,0:16:14.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It seemed like you had something to tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.86,0:16:19.08,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I'm sure you know, but it'd be best \Nto seal away that orb.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.08,0:16:20.89,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll propose the idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.36,0:16:28.04,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,On that note, why didn't you take the orb \Nout of Farsas after casting that curse?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.04,0:16:31.96,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I knew not where it was, \Nnor did I wish to search for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.96,0:16:36.57,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,But seeing as how that idiot used it, \Nyou know its whereabouts now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.57,0:16:38.83,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It appears to be in the treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.83,0:16:41.98,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But the orb he used is the one in Tuldarr.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.98,0:16:43.50,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Tuldarr?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.50,0:16:45.19,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,There's more than one?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.94,0:16:49.47,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,How much do you know about those orbs?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.47,0:16:51.88,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I could ask you the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.88,0:16:55.77,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I got it from a traveling fortune teller, \Naround two hundred years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.16,0:16:57.55,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I was told that with the conviction,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.55,0:17:01.62,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,you can go back in time to change \Nthe past with that magic implement.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.62,0:17:03.98,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Conviction, you say...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.39,0:17:09.46,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What I know is that the magic \Nspheres are known as Eleterria,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.46,0:17:11.58,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,and most likely there exist two of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.58,0:17:15.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The other one is under \Nseal in Tuldarr's treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.05,0:17:18.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,And there's a man who seeks to possess both.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.11,0:17:24.23,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,That man is most likely \Nthe one who told me about you two.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.50,0:17:26.09,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What? Valt did?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.09,0:17:27.85,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Take great caution.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.85,0:17:30.73,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Men like him won't hesitate \Nto do whatever it takes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.37,0:17:34.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm grateful for your warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.10,0:17:42.04,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,I'll be taking my leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.04,0:17:43.22,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Please wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.12,0:17:48.77,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Distorting the past and sacrificing \Nyourself to save someone...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.77,0:17:51.34,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Do you really think that's a sin?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.73,0:17:58.80,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,No matter how much you love someone, \Nyou mustn't change the way things should be,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.80,0:18:02.11,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,to say nothing of \Nsacrificing yourself to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.11,0:18:04.14,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,The very height of foolishness.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.84,0:18:07.35,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,You should know, as the one who was saved.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.50,0:18:12.56,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Excellent job breaking that curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.06,0:18:17.93,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,The definition name just serves to protect \Nthat idiot while sealing away his memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.93,0:18:19.20,Default,Lavinia,0,0,0,,Pay it no mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.74,0:18:22.31,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.82,0:18:34.34,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,How are you feeling?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.34,0:18:36.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,A lot better now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.81,0:18:39.07,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I forced you into a really demanding battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.50,0:18:40.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Sorry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.80,0:18:45.72,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,To be honest, I might have lost even \Nif I hadn't been watching out for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.72,0:18:47.39,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She was that strong?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.88,0:18:49.78,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,We were up against a witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.19,0:18:52.82,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I only managed to break \Nher spell by sheer luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.32,0:18:58.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What's more, it felt like she was \Nholding back the entire time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.26,0:19:00.38,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.97,0:19:06.83,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha, I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.81,0:19:09.07,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,About what?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.53,0:19:11.29,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Four hundred years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.29,0:19:11.93,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.29,0:19:15.03,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Why are {\i1}you{\i0} the one apologizing?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.03,0:19:18.16,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I mean, I'm sure you must have your grievances.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.79,0:19:24.01,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Like why I decided to change the past, \Nor why I disappeared afterwards.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.01,0:19:25.39,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I wouldn't dare...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.73,0:19:34.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Until I was thirteen, \Nthe world I knew was very small.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.54,0:19:38.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I was taken to the castle \Nright after I was born
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.21,0:19:40.56,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,and raised as the future queen candidate.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.04,0:19:45.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The only one I could call family \Nwas the other candidate to be ruler.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.94,0:19:50.79,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The person I considered a brother \Nchose to sever ties with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.69,0:19:56.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It was then that {\i1}he{\i0} came into \Nmy life and taught me so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.01,0:19:59.79,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I was happy every day I spent with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.22,0:20:02.99,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Not only did he save my life,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.33,0:20:07.36,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,he showed me the love I needed \Nto walk onward by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.62,0:20:12.58,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But when I came to this era \Nto try and repay him,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.58,0:20:16.35,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,you turned out to be vicious and unkind to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.35,0:20:18.45,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,unfriendly to foreign citizens,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.45,0:20:20.97,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,blind to your own faults \Nbut critical of others...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.74,0:20:22.13,Default-Top,Oscar,0,0,0,,Hey, what's all this now?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.13,0:20:24.70,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But that unrelenting side \Nis what I like about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.18,0:20:29.91,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The you that's here now \Nis the one I want to stay with.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.04,0:20:37.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's why...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.59,0:20:39.83,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm very happy now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.00,0:20:42.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.39,0:20:58.59,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You're always there to save me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.76,0:21:04.01,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Should you ever grow weak, or lose your magic,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.47,0:21:06.35,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll be there to compensate and protect you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.76,0:21:10.43,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Whatever you may lose, I'll provide for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.30,0:21:12.42,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.91,0:21:18.95,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be the one to protect you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.74,0:22:55.93,Default,Aurelia,0,0,0,,Listen here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.93,0:22:58.21,Default,Aurelia,0,0,0,,Try your best not to cause any problems.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.21,0:23:01.24,Default,Aurelia,0,0,0,,This ceremony is a birthday \Ncelebration for the king of Farsas!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.24,0:23:02.11,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.51,0:23:05.06,Default,Aurelia,0,0,0,,Do you really?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.27,0:23:13.16,Default,Aurelia,0,0,0,,What's wrong, Travis?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.16,0:23:14.66,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I'll be right there.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.66,0:23:16.99,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,By the way, the ribbon in your hair is loose.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.99,0:23:18.77,Default,Aurelia,0,0,0,,Wh-What?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.94,0:23:24.46,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,See? There we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.84,0:23:27.67,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Your beauty is unmatched, Aurelia.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.08,0:23:30.51,Default,Aurelia,0,0,0,,Spare me the inane flattery.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.51,0:23:32.38,Default,Aurelia,0,0,0,,Just don't do anything stupid.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.47,0:23:40.02,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Half of Eternity ~
